; Every node's span, read back out of the source it points at.
;
; `span_dump --cst` prints one line per node: the node's constructor and the text
; between its span's two positions. `span_dump --sst` does the same over the
; desugared tree and prints each node's variant as well, so its expectations
; show the rewrites of docs/design/desugaring.md having happened and not merely that
; spans survived them.
;
; The goldens' purpose: a span is only ever wrong by pointing at the wrong text,
; and the rest of the suite cannot see where. The acceptance tests ask whether a file
; parses, and the grouping tests ask which shape it parsed to -- neither reads
; a position. So a grammar change that widens a span to swallow a binder, or
; narrows one past its own bracket, passes everything, and only a reviewer
; may catch it.
;
; A failing diff is not by itself a bug: a change to the grammar, the fixture
; or the lowering is expected to move these. Read the diff, satisfy yourself
; that each moved span still covers what its node stands for and that each
; rewrite still produces the shape it should, and promote it with
; `dune promote`.
;
; Three fixtures. `main.zn` is the fixture the parser suite already reaches
; for, and it covers the breadth of the grammar. `fixtures/utf8.zn` covers the
; only input class `main.zn` does not: spans are byte offsets, and while a
; file is ASCII a code-point offset is indistinguishable from a byte one. They
; diverge at the first multibyte character and every span after it shifts --
; which is exactly the bug found on #86, after the suite had been green
; through it.
;
; `fixtures/desugar.zn` is the third, and unlike the other two it was written for these
; tests: every rewrite in docs/design/desugaring.md 2 appears in it at least once.
; The other two do not manage that -- `main.zn` reaches only two of the five
; derived operators, so three of them had no expectation anywhere.

; The two structure renderings, which name every field rather than printing a
; span. `lib/cst/to_tree_graph.ml` had no test of any kind before this -- five
; hundred lines reached only by the compiler binary -- and its SST counterpart
; would have inherited that. Rendering one fixture through each covers both.
;
; Reading them side by side is also the clearest statement of the
; desugaring's rewrites: the SST rendering is the CST rendering with `parenthized`,
; `ret_shorthand`, `var_decl_shorthand`, `trailing` and one of the two call
; groups gone.

; How a rejected file is reported: the source line, the caret under the
; offending text, and the message. Every other test in the suite checks only
; whether a file was rejected, so a change to the renderer in lib/diagnostic/
; -- a caret one column off after a tab or a multibyte character, a message
; lost on the way out -- would pass it unseen.
;
; One fixture per way the parse can fail, each reaching a different producer:
; `syntax.zn` the parser itself, after a tab and multibyte text on the same
; line; `lexing.zn` a character no token starts with; `malformed-utf8.zn` a
; byte that is not UTF-8; `rejected.zn` a grammar action; `statement.zn`
; the statement check that walks the finished tree, whose span is empty; and
; `recovery.zn` several syntax errors in one file, each reported because the
; parse restarts at the next declaration after a failure (lib/cst/parse.ml).

; The rules themselves are written from the golden files by
; tests/gen/gen_rules.ml, into dune.inc. A fixture added without its rules
; fails the diff below; `dune promote` then writes them.

(include dune.inc)

(rule
 (deps (glob_files golden/*) (source_tree fixtures))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc.gen
   (run %{exe:../gen/gen_rules.exe} parser))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff dune.inc dune.inc.gen)))
